    "validator_version": "1",
    "note": "Reviewed German fragments. The model SELECTS codes from this file; it never writes prose and never writes a number. Every {SLOT} is a fact id the renderer fills from typed, persisted values. No probability language, no advice, no certainty. max_width values are REVIEWED bounds used by the worst-case fit test, not measurements of current values. v3.4 adds rule-bound operations headlines, compact caveats, and the bounded trigger/current disclosure required when an active condition materially changes before send. v3.3 is left byte-identical because phrase versions are immutable registry identities. v3.5 carries every fragment in two languages, German (the reviewed v3.4 text, byte-for-byte) and English; the operator selects the rendered language with MESSAGE_LANGUAGE and both languages are held to the worst-case fit. Codes, slots, priorities and facts are unchanged from v3.4.",
